"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[64499],{664499:e=>{e.exports="# How to create or edit resource (datasource, rule, case, alert, query)\n\n## Approach\n\nDo **not** try to complete create or edit in chat (e.g. by filling every field via tools). Instead:\n\n- **Create:** Navigate to the creation page with the matching **create-\\*** intent and set **continueMessage** so the page agent continues (e.g. “User wants to create a new datasource. Help them through the creation flow.”).\n- **Edit:** If you don’t have the resource ID, use **how-to-find-resource** to resolve it. Then navigate to the **edit/view page** with the matching **view-\\*** intent, **resourceId**, and **continueMessage** (e.g. “User wants to edit this datasource. Help them with transformations and settings.”). The page-specific agent will take over with full edit capabilities.\n\n## Create datasource\n\n| Step            | Action                                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Intent          | `create-datasource`                                                                                            |\n| resourceType    | `datasource`                                                                                                   |\n| resourceId      | `null`                                                                                                         |\n| Route           | `/configure/datasources/create`                                                                                |\n| continueMessage | e.g. “User wants to create a new datasource. Help them configure data ingestion through the ingestion wizard.” |\n\nUse **navigateWithinLakewatch** with the above. Ask the user to configure data ingestion through the ingestion wizard on the create page.\n\n## Create detection rule\n\n| Step            | Action                                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Intent          | `create-rule`                                                                                                 |\n| resourceType    | `rule`                                                                                                        |\n| resourceId      | `null`                                                                                                        |\n| Route           | `/configure/detection-rules/add`                                                                              |\n| continueMessage | e.g. “User wants to create a new detection rule. Help them through the wizard.” (so the page agent continues) |\n\nUse **navigateWithinLakewatch** with the above. The Configure → Detection rules add page and its agent will take over.\n\n## Create query\n\nFor **query**, creation is done via the **apiCreateLakewatchQuery** tool (title + initial SQL); then open the new query and hand off to the page agent.\n\n| Step | Action                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 1    | Call **apiCreateLakewatchQuery** with title and initialSql (use the user’s if provided, or placeholders like “New query” and “” otherwise).            |\n| 2    | Navigate with intent `view-query`, resourceType `query`, resourceId = the **queryId** returned from apiCreateLakewatchQuery.                           |\n| 3    | Set **continueMessage** to the user’s intent (e.g. “User wanted to create a new query; help them edit and run it.”) so the query page agent continues. |\n\nThe query page agent will continue the conversation on the opened query.\n\n## Edit resource (datasource, rule, case, alert, query)\n\nWhen the user wants to **edit**, **update**, or **work on** an existing resource, redirect them to the resource’s edit/view page so the page-specific agent can help with full capabilities.\n\n| Step | Action                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 1    | **Resolve the resource ID** if you don’t have it: use **how-to-find-resource** (list by name, filter, or get by ID).                                                                                               |\n| 2    | **Navigate** with **navigateWithinLakewatch**: use the **view-\\*** intent for that resource type, set **resourceId** to the resolved ID, and set **continueMessage** to the user’s edit goal.                      |\n| 3    | The **destination page agent** (datasource authoring, detection rule authoring, case manage, alert manage, or query authoring) receives the continueMessage and continues the conversation with edit UI and tools. |\n\n### Edit by resource type\n\n| Resource       | Intent               | resourceType    | resourceId   | continueMessage example                                                                        |\n| -------------- | -------------------- | --------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Datasource     | `view-datasource`    | `datasource`    | datasourceId | “User wants to edit this datasource. Help them with transformations or settings.”              |\n| Detection rule | `view-rule`          | `rule`          | ruleId       | “User wants to edit this detection rule. Help them with SQL, observables, or schedule.”        |\n| Security case  | `view-security-case` | `security-case` | caseId       | “User wants to work on this security case. Help them update state, assignee, or add comments.” |\n| System case    | `view-system-case`   | `system-case`   | caseId       | “User wants to work on this system case. Help them with state or details.”                     |\n| Query          | `view-query`         | `query`         | queryId      | “User wants to edit this query. Help them modify SQL or run it.”                               |\n\nNever try to perform edits in chat when the user could do them on the page—redirect so the page agent can use the full UI and tools.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Create:** Use **navigateWithinLakewatch** with **create-\\*** intent, resourceId `null`, and **continueMessage**. For query, use **apiCreateLakewatchQuery** first, then navigate with **view-query** and the new queryId.\n- **Edit:** Resolve resource ID (**how-to-find-resource** if needed), then **navigateWithinLakewatch** with **view-\\*** intent, **resourceId**, and **continueMessage** so the page-specific agent continues with full edit capabilities.\n\nFor exact intent names and routes, use **how-to-navigation**. For finding a resource by name or ID, use **how-to-find-resource**.\n"}}]);
